abstract: >-
  Self-contained MATLAB code for the moon-based geometric calibration of a 180-degree
  all-sky airglow imager and for the subsequent 250 km airglow projection. The method
  targets long-exposure (180 s) archival airglow data in which stars cannot be reliably
  extracted, and explicitly decouples the degeneracy among the zenith pixel, the
  azimuthal orientation angle and the radial scale. Includes the calibration pipeline,
  the geometric projection, plasma-bubble detection, synthetic positive controls, and a
  verification script that reproduces every numerical value printed in the paper from the
  bundled calibration files (no raw data required).
